  "scope": {
    "consumer": "Existing single-unpack INI_SET Iterator bridge; ordinary CV and admitted emitted temporary routes retain their current source/owner guards.",
    "values": "A68 scalars plus finite path-acyclic CFG-admitted ARRAY and ordinary non-Stringable root INSTANCE values, from KNOWN current or genuine BYREF cells. Existing A67 instance/static type-source checks are unchanged.",
    "ownership": "Normalized config_pack_prefix/config_nodes call slots own copied values once. Array COW preserves table snapshots; embedded aliases and object properties stay shared. Slots survive next and DATA/INPUT retirement, then use ordinary CONFIG_INVOKE/API and argument cleanup. API TypeError TraceArgs may retain the arguments, including the Iterator itself.",
    "abrupt": "Exact owning send-check and admitted primitive-key Error producers keep their task for THROW_SEARCH. CURRENT releases before DATA/INPUT, then the copied prefix; outside cache owners defer destruction. Live ownership checks are disjoint and require allocated roots.",
    "history": "ITEMS and retired CURRENT records carry bounded structural identities, not live recursive graph checks. Authenticated key/send retirement cannot reconstruct old BYREF contents. Other retired callback stages retain a nonempty copied-prefix witness. This is structural history, not a provenance-complete reachability certificate.",
    "limits": [
      "Stringable/effectful conversion and other CONFIG/Generator value consumers remain separate.",
      "Normal capture/send retains existing finite graph, materialized/special-cell and transient authority restrictions; constructed cycle Error checks do not claim normal cyclic sends or wider GC coverage.",
      "Existing last-owner/temporary INPUT finalizer predicates still apply; an unadmitted effectful last INPUT remains Unsupported.",
      "All held boundaries remain unchanged, including Source47 low-precision DEFINE-name NaN and owned-NUL release."
    ]
  },
